        <body>
            <div xml:id="d389">

                <pb facs="0587" n="493" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg493"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McKenzie to Mr. Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Lima,
                                Peru</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1896-07-20"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 20, 1896</hi></date>. (Received Aug.
                        13.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 307.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith,
                    payable to your order, a bill of exchange on New York, No. 67, for $2,415.46,
                    United States currency, at thirty days’ sight, being proceeds of a draft for
                    5,000 silver soles handed to me by the Peruvian Government in part payment of
                    the 10,000 soles due this year in settlement of the Amazonas claim, together
                    with my note of May 20, 1896, to the Peruvian minister for foreign affairs, and
                    his reply, with a translation; also a note from Mr. D. Pattison, of the house of
                    W. R. Grace &amp; Co., Lima, together with quotations of current rates of
                    exchange, and my note of July 18, 1896, to the minister for foreign affairs,
                    etc., all of which are self-explanatory.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. A. McKenzie.</hi></signed></closer>




